[Music]  how did a real-life cowboy go from rodeo  shows to appearing in midnight texas how  did that same actor land on just about  every western and quasi-western movie  and television show for the last 20  years let's dive into the long and  varied career of fourie j smith  there's a reason why the wise rugged  lloyd pierce on yellowstone imbues his  scenes with such an air of realism as it  turns out the actor behind the longtime  dutton employee for e.j smith is a  real-life cowboy with decades of  experience under his large buckled belt  that experience served him well as both  a stuntman and an actor and throughout  his decades-long career in show business  smith has been back in the saddle more  times than one could count this perhaps  is why the charismatic and occasionally  mysterious lloyd pierce looks so  familiar to viewers beginning in the  late 1980s the actor found himself  starring in several television movies tv  series and films and in each one managed  to prove that as a performer he was no  one trick pony no room for outcasts like  us in the bunk house  by 1993 40j smith had several off-screen  and minor roles under his belt he was  mostly known for his work as a stuntman  in rambo 3 when he took on the role of  pony deal in writer kevin jarre's  tombstone the film told the story of  gunslingers and occasional lawmen wyatt  earp and doc holliday's involvement in  the infamous 1881 shootout at the ok  corral in tombstone arizona the movie's  cast was stacked with a-listers but even  among the superstars smith managed to  make an impression with future casting  directors at least though smith's role  in the film was as a non-speaking  ensemble member of the criminal clanton  gang the film's success helped the  experienced stuntman showcase his stage  skills  four years after his role as a  rambunctious cowboy and tombstone 4 aj  smith starred alongside javier bartom  rosie perez and james gandolfini in  director alex de iglesia's critically  acclaimed dark comedy perdita durango  strutting onto the scene smith's  armendars attempts to negotiate with a  fellow criminal before being killed in a  shootout although the scene is  relatively short it allowed smith to  fully embrace and embody a character  with some semblance of a backstory the  film's cult status helped the already  prolific and in-demand additional crew  cowboy flex his acting chops the year  prior smith had starred in a short scene  in the made for tv movie ruby gene and  joe wherein he delivered a few drunken  lines at a birthday party before getting  punched in the face by tom selleck still  it was hardly as big an on-screen moment  for the actor as his shootout in perdita  durango  though for aj smith's screen time in  duncan tucker's oscar-nominated  transamerica was short his dialogue in  the scene acts as a catalyst for a  critical moment for the film's  protagonists in the movie a religious  conservative woman named dabri who is  saving up for sex reassignment surgery  is compelled by her therapist to track  down the son she unknowingly fathered  while still in college brie heads to new  york to track down her son but since she  is unable to explain the true nature of  her relationship to the street hustler  teen she pretends to be a christian  caseworker the two embark on a  cross-country journey back to la and  along the way stop at a roadside market  in arizona called sami's wigwam smith  plays sammy who assumes the angsty teen  is the woman's child and when toby  swears it breathe smith's character  chastises him you watch your mouth  around your mouth she is not my mother  she's not anyone's mother she's not even  a real woman it's an important moment in  developing the character's relationship  and vindicates bree's fears and her  motivations for lying to toby while  illustrating that the two very much  already come off as a parenting child  smith's success following his role in  transamerica is proof that sometimes  it's more about quality than quantity  when it comes to screen time  by 2017 for ej smith had established  himself as the man to call when casting  directors were looking for a real-life  wrangler and horseman who also knew how  to deliver a line in 2013 he provided  his animal wrangler skills to the crew  of two guns in 2016 he worked with  future yellowstone creator taylor  sheridan as an animal wrangler on the  oscar-nominated heller high water while  one would be hard-pressed to recognize  smith in either film he had a more  visible role in the breaking bad  spin-off better call saul in the season  3 episode mabel smith stars as the  junkyard owner of 5j's auto salvage who  loans mics and tools in space to work  in 2018 for ej smith lent his  charismatic western aesthetic to nbc's  midnight texas  the town of midnight is a safe place for  outsiders who fit the category mainly  based on their supernatural  characteristics among that cast of  outsiders is former were tiger and now  cured reverend emilio sheehan in the  episode to witch hell and back viewers  learn the origin of sheen's identity and  watch as he struggles to come to terms  with his past smith appears in the  flashback as the real reverend emilio  sheehan a priest and cowboy who was  killed by the transformed were tiger  years ago when the weretiger transformed  into his human self again he took on the  priest's identity racked with guilt and  determined to atone smith's real-life  experience clearly helps him get across  the rugged realism of the characters he  plays that seems to be true whether he's  being attacked by a were tiger or doing  the dudn's dirty work on yellowstone  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite actors are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

